# DTF tier manifest: search-gin-2871
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. No SSO or object storage needed -- the
# oracle drives the real public HTTP search path (/search/quick, /search/advanced)
# plus DB truth (docker exec psql) against the artifacts.search_vector column.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#2871, PF-009, epic #2516): artifact full-text search used to
# filter on an inline functional predicate
#   to_tsvector('english', name || ' ' || path || ' ' || COALESCE(version,''))
#     @@ to_tsquery('english', $1)
# with nothing on `artifacts` matching it, so every /search request Parallel
# Seq Scanned the table recomputing to_tsvector per row (twice, counting the
# pagination COUNT). The fix adds a trigger-maintained `search_vector tsvector`
# column, a partial GIN index (WHERE is_deleted=false), and rewrites both search
# queries + the COUNT to filter on the stored column.
#
# Discriminating oracle (both DB truth AND behavior):
#   * The stored column, its BEFORE INSERT/UPDATE trigger, and the partial GIN
#     index must exist. On a pre-#2871 image the `search_vector` column does not
#     exist, so these checks RED-fail; on the fixed image they GREEN-pass.
#   * Semantics must be preserved exactly: quick and advanced search return the
#     SAME ordered result set for the same term, the advanced total count is
#     exact, prefix match is honored, a tsquery-metacharacter term returns an
#     empty result with HTTP 200 (not 500), unrelated artifacts are excluded,
#     and a freshly uploaded artifact is immediately searchable with its stored
#     search_vector populated by the trigger.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
